title: Women's Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: lwusp_in_government = 1 and womens_rights_timer = 0
on-arrival: womens_rights_timer += 10; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/monica.jpg
frequency: 50
max-visits: 6

= Women's Rights

According to the Constitution, women are equal to men, but this is not followed in practice. Women in the workforce are not paid equally for the same work, in addition to often being pushed out of employment after marriage. Men are still favored in marriage and family policy, and there are restrictions on women's rights in many other domains. And that is not to mention the overwhelming patriarchal culture present in Sordland.

Lately, feminist movements have started to gain great popularity in Sordland, and many people in our faction have declared themselves in favor of women's rights.

- @labor: Institute policies that help women in the workforce.
- @family: Reform marriage, divorce, and property law.
- @welfare: Improve welfare for single mothers and children.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@labor
subtitle: Paid maternal leave policies, equal pay policies, and so on.
on-arrival: womens_work += 1; womens_rights += 1; workers_lwusp -= 4 if unemployed > 15; new_middle_lwusp += 4*(1-dissent); workers_lwusp += 4*(1 - dissent); economic_growth += 0.1
max-visits: 3

These policies mean that our party is increasing in popularity among the "new women" who work outside the home. [? if unemployed > 15 : However, many male workers develop a backlash towards women in the workplace, especially given the rising unemployment. ?]

@family
subtitle: Change family and inheritance law to treat women more equally.
on-arrival: family_law += 1; womens_rights += 1; new_middle_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent); workers_lwusp += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_lwusp -= 2; rural_lwusp -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_usp_coalition; rwusp_relation -= 5
max-visits: 2

These policies aim to ensure that women have equal rights within a marriage, including the right to divorce. The more conservative segments of society treat our reforms as deleterious to the social fabric.

@welfare
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: welfare += 1; workers_lwusp += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_lwusp += 5*(1-dissent); budget -= 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare >= 1 and unemployed >= 15 and in_usp_coalition; unemployed -= 0.4; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.3; rwusp_relation -= 5; nfp_relation -= 5

We have increased welfare spending on women and children. [? if welfare >= 1 and unemployed >= 15 : Some of our coalition partners consider increased welfare spending profligate at this time. ?]
